    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\r\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\r\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\r\n    <span class=\"time\">45 min</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\r\n    <span class=\"chip\">Heap / Priority Queue</span>\r\n  </div>\r\n  <h1>Two heaps and k-way merge</h1>\r\n  <p class=\"lead\">Two heaps that face each other answer \"what is the middle right now?\" in O(log n) per change. The same trick, with a hash map for lazy deletion, slides a median window. A heap plus a sorted array runs greedy picks with two keys (IPO, hiring), and a heap of heads merges k sorted streams (merge k lists, smallest range, k smallest pairs). This page builds each one step by step, with templates in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\r\n"
